    "chunk_text": "Facilities Managers (also known in India as Department Head, In-charge) is a professional in the Management & Leadership domain. Plan, direct, or coordinate operations and functionalities of facilities and buildings. May include surrounding grounds or multiple facilities of an organization's campus. Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Strategic Planning, Leadership, Decision Making, Communication, Financial Acumen, Team Management, Negotiation, Problem Solving, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Business Administration, Finance, Human Resources, Operations Management, Organizational Behavior. This career suits enterprising and leadership-driven personalities who are leadership-oriented, decisive, results-driven. Management roles in India require an MBA from IIMs or top B-schools. PSU management positions available via UPSC/state exams. Strong demand in IT services, BFSI, manufacturing, and e-commerce sectors. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b912\u201314 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b915\u201345 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b945\u201390+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Mumbai, Delhi, Bengaluru, Hyderabad; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
