    "extractedSkillsCount": 10,
    "description": "",
    "chunk_text": "Accountants and Auditors in India commonly correspond to Chartered Accountants (CA), a highly respected professional qualification governed by the Institute of Chartered Accountants of India. Chartered Accountants manage financial reporting, auditing, taxation, and strategic financial advisory for companies, governments, and individuals. Their daily responsibilities typically include auditing corporate financial statements, preparing tax returns and advising on tax planning, conducting financial analysis for business decisions, ensuring compliance with regulatory standards such as Companies Act and GST laws, and advising organizations on financial restructuring or risk management. Essential skills include financial analysis, accounting proficiency, taxation expertise, analytical reasoning, attention to detail, problem solving, business communication, regulatory interpretation, auditing techniques, and strategic thinking. Important knowledge areas include financial accounting, corporate taxation, auditing standards, business law, and financial management. Work style requires discipline, precision, and ethical responsibility, fitting investigative and conventional personalities who enjoy working with complex financial systems and regulations. In India entry occurs through the CA pathway of CA Foundation, CA Intermediate, and CA Final exams along with mandatory articleship training lasting several years; the journey typically takes five to six years and is considered one of the most rigorous commerce qualifications. Starting salaries for newly qualified CAs generally range from 8\u201312 LPA, rising to 18\u201330 LPA mid-career and exceeding 50 LPA for partners or senior finance leaders. Major opportunities exist in cities such as Mumbai, Delhi, Bengaluru, and Hyderabad. Internationally the CA qualification is recognized in global finance, consulting, and multinational corporations, often enabling pathways into CFO roles, consulting firms, or global accounting networks.",
