    "chunk_text": "Computer Network Architects (also known in India as Design Architect, Project Architect) is a professional in the Information Technology & Computing domain. Design and implement computer and information networks, such as local area networks (LAN), wide area networks (WAN), intranets, extranets, and other data communications networks. Perform network model... Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Programming, Algorithms, Data Structures, System Design, Problem Solving, Database Management, Cloud Computing, DevOps, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Computer Science, Mathematics, Software Engineering, Database Systems, Networking. This career suits investigative and analytical personalities who are logical, detail-oriented, innovative. India is the world's largest IT outsourcing hub. IITs and NITs are top institutes. GATE score used for PSU (ISRO, CDAC, NIC) recruitment. Bengaluru is the Silicon Valley of India. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b96\u20138 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b99\u201330 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b930\u201370+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Pune, Chennai; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
