    "chunk_text": "Electrical, Mechanical, and Industrial Engineers in Indian Public Sector Undertakings commonly work as PSU Engineers in organizations such as BHEL, ONGC, BPCL, and NTPC. These professionals design, operate, and maintain large-scale industrial systems including power plants, oil refineries, heavy machinery, and national energy infrastructure. Daily responsibilities include supervising plant operations and maintenance, designing engineering solutions to improve efficiency, managing large technical projects, analyzing equipment performance data, and coordinating with contractors and regulatory authorities to ensure safety and compliance. Core skills include engineering design, problem solving, project management, data analysis, systems thinking, teamwork, technical communication, maintenance planning, safety management, and analytical reasoning. Knowledge areas include mechanical or electrical engineering principles, thermodynamics, industrial systems, power generation technologies, and energy management. The work style favors reliability, analytical thinking, and structured operations, suiting realistic and investigative personalities interested in large infrastructure systems. In India entry is typically through high GATE scores followed by recruitment in PSUs such as NTPC, ONGC, BPCL, and BHEL. Most recruits hold B.Tech degrees from engineering colleges including IITs, NITs, and reputable state engineering institutions. Starting salaries range roughly from 12\u201315 LPA including allowances, rising to 25\u201335 LPA in senior managerial engineering roles with excellent job stability and benefits. Work is concentrated near industrial hubs and energy centers such as Mumbai, Bengaluru, Chennai, Hyderabad, and various plant locations across India.",
