    "chunk_text": "Engineering Technologists and Technicians, Except Drafters, All Other (also known in India as Technical Expert, Sr. Engineer) is a professional in the Architecture & Engineering domain. All engineering technologists and technicians, except drafters, not listed separately. Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Technical Drawing, CAD Software, Engineering Analysis, Project Management, Problem Solving, Mathematics, Simulation Software, Quality Control, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Engineering Principles, Physics, Mathematics, Materials Science, Design. This career suits realistic and hands-on personalities who are methodical, technically precise, innovative. Engineering remains a top career in India. IITs/NITs are premier institutes. GATE is mandatory for PSU recruitment and M.Tech admission. ISRO, DRDO, BARC, BHEL, NTPC are major PSU employers. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b94\u20136 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b97\u201320 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b920\u201345+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Delhi, Mumbai, Pune, Chennai; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
