    "chunk_text": "Rehabilitation Counselors (also known in India as Guidance Counselor, Psychologist) is a professional in the Social Services & Community domain. Counsel individuals to maximize the independence and employability of persons coping with personal, social, and vocational difficulties that result from birth defects, illness, disease, accidents, agi... Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Counseling, Communication, Empathy, Case Management, Community Outreach, Report Writing, Crisis Intervention, Cultural Sensitivity, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Social Work, Psychology, Sociology, Public Policy, Community Development. This career suits social and helping personalities who are empathetic, patient, service-oriented. Social services in India offered through government departments, NGOs, and international organizations. TISS Mumbai, Delhi School of Social Work are top institutes. UPSC/State PSC for government social welfare roles. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b93\u20135 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b96\u201312 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b912\u201322+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Delhi, Mumbai, Kolkata, Hyderabad; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
