    "chunk_text": "Precision Agriculture Technicians (also known in India as Technical Officer, Field Technician) is a professional in the Agriculture, Forestry & Fishing domain. Apply geospatial technologies, including geographic information systems (GIS) and Global Positioning System (GPS), to agricultural production or management activities, such as pest scouting, site-spec... Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Research Methodology, Data Analysis, Scientific Writing, Laboratory Techniques, Statistical Analysis, Critical Thinking, Literature Review, Grant Writing, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Scientific Domain Expertise, Statistics, Research Ethics, Scientific Communication, Methodology. This career suits investigative and analytical personalities who are curious, patient, detail-oriented. Science research in India mainly through government institutions: CSIR, DST, ISRO, DRDO. CSIR-NET/GATE required for research fellowships. IISc, IISERs, TIFR are top research institutes. Biocon, Dr. Reddy's for applied research. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b94\u20136 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b97\u201318 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b918\u201335+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Delhi, Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Pune; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
