    "description": "Provide social services and assistance to improve the social and psychological functioning of children and their families and to maximize the family well-being and the academic functioning of children. May assist parents, arrange adoptions, and find foster homes for abandoned or abused children. In schools, they address such problems as teenage pregnancy, misbehavior, and truancy. May also advise teachers.",
    "chunk_text": "Child, Family, and School Social Workers (also known in India as Sr. Child, Family, and School Social Workers, Child, Family, and School Social Workers Executive) is a professional in the Social Services & Community domain. Provide social services and assistance to improve the social and psychological functioning of children and their families and to maximize the family well-being and the academic functioning of children... Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Counseling, Communication, Empathy, Case Management, Community Outreach, Report Writing, Crisis Intervention, Cultural Sensitivity, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Social Work, Psychology, Sociology, Public Policy, Community Development. This career suits social and helping personalities who are empathetic, patient, service-oriented. Social services in India offered through government departments, NGOs, and international organizations. TISS Mumbai, Delhi School of Social Work are top institutes. UPSC/State PSC for government social welfare roles. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b93\u20135 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b96\u201312 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b912\u201322+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Delhi, Mumbai, Kolkata, Hyderabad; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
