    "chunk_text": "Merchandise Displayers and Window Trimmers (also known in India as Sr. Merchandise Displayers and Window Trimmers, Merchandise Displayers and Window Trimmers Executive) is a professional in the Sales & Retail domain. Plan and erect commercial displays, such as those in windows and interiors of retail stores and at trade exhibitions. Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Creativity, Design Software, Visual Communication, Storytelling, Portfolio Development, Typography, Color Theory, Collaboration, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Design Principles, Art History, Digital Tools, Communication Theory, Cultural Studies. This career suits artistic and creative personalities who are creative, expressive, collaborative. Creative fields in India are growing rapidly with OTT expansion, gaming industry, and digital marketing. NID Ahmedabad, NIFT, FTII Pune are premier institutions. Mumbai and Hyderabad dominate film/media. Freelancing is common. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b93\u20135 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b96\u201318 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b918\u201340+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Mumbai, Delhi, Bengaluru, Hyderabad; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
