    "chunk_text": "Tutors (also known in India as Sr. Tutors, Tutors Executive) is a professional in the Education & Training domain. Instruct individual students or small groups of students in academic subjects to support formal class instruction or to prepare students for standardized or admissions tests. Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Teaching, Curriculum Design, Communication, Patience, Subject Knowledge, Assessment, Classroom Management, Mentoring, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Pedagogy, Subject Matter, Psychology, Educational Policy, Assessment Methods. This career suits social and helping personalities who are patient, communicative, empathetic. Teaching in India requires B.Ed degree for K-12 and UGC-NET for university lecturers. CTET/State TET mandatory for government school teachers. EdTech boom (BYJU'S, Unacademy) created new opportunities. KVS and NVS are central government school networks. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b93\u20135 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b96\u201314 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b914\u201328+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Delhi, Mumbai, Kolkata, Chennai; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
