    "education_required": "PhD",
    "transitionHorizonMonths": 6,
    "baseSuitabilityScore": 85,
    "extractedSkillsCount": 10,
    "description": "",
    "chunk_text": "Postsecondary Professors in engineering and science in India correspond to roles such as IIT Professor, NIT Professor, or research faculty at institutions like IISc and central universities. These professionals conduct advanced research, teach undergraduate and postgraduate students, and contribute to scientific innovation and academic knowledge. Typical daily activities include delivering lectures and mentoring students, supervising research scholars and PhD candidates, publishing research papers in international journals, writing grant proposals for research funding, and collaborating with industry or government research programs. Essential skills include research methodology, analytical thinking, teaching ability, academic writing, mentorship, presentation skills, critical thinking, subject expertise, project management, and collaboration. Core knowledge areas include advanced subject specialization in engineering or science fields, statistics and research methods, academic publishing standards, and higher education pedagogy. Work style emphasizes curiosity, persistence, intellectual independence, and mentorship, suiting investigative and social personalities who enjoy deep learning and knowledge creation. In India the pathway typically involves completing a PhD (often 5\u20136 years) after a bachelor\u2019s and master\u2019s degree, followed by qualifying exams such as UGC NET or institute-specific faculty recruitment processes. Fresh faculty earn around 12\u201315 LPA including allowances, rising to 25\u201340+ LPA equivalent for senior professors and research chairs. Work is concentrated in academic hubs such as Bengaluru, Delhi, Mumbai, Chennai, and Kanpur. Internationally academic research careers are globally transferable with opportunities in universities and research institutes worldwide.",
