    "chunk_text": "General Internal Medicine Physicians (also known in India as Sr. General Internal Medicine Physicians, General Internal Medicine Physicians Executive) is a professional in the Healthcare & Medical domain. Diagnose and provide nonsurgical treatment for a wide range of diseases and injuries of internal organ systems. Provide care mainly for adults and adolescents, and are based primarily in an outpatient... Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Clinical Assessment, Diagnosis, Patient Communication, Medical Procedures, Critical Thinking, Empathy, Documentation, Research, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Anatomy, Physiology, Pathology, Pharmacology, Clinical Medicine. This career suits social and helping personalities who are empathetic, detail-oriented, under-pressure. Healthcare is a top career in India. NEET-UG required for MBBS/BDS/BAMS admissions. AIIMS Delhi/Mumbai, CMC Vellore, JIPMER are top institutes. Private hospital chains and government health services are major employers. Abroad opportunities via USMLE/PLAB. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b95\u20137 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b98\u201330 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b930\u201370+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Mumbai, Delhi, Chennai, Hyderabad; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
