    "baseSuitabilityScore": 85,
    "extractedSkillsCount": 10,
    "description": "Edit moving images on film, video, or other media. May work with a producer or director to organize images for final production. May edit or synchronize soundtracks with images.",
    "chunk_text": "Film and Video Editors (also known in India as Sr. Film and Video Editors, Film and Video Editors Executive) is a professional in the Management & Leadership domain. Edit moving images on film, video, or other media. May work with a producer or director to organize images for final production. May edit or synchronize soundtracks with images. Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Creativity, Design Software, Visual Communication, Storytelling, Portfolio Development, Typography, Color Theory, Collaboration, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Design Principles, Art History, Digital Tools, Communication Theory, Cultural Studies. This career suits artistic and creative personalities who are creative, expressive, collaborative. Creative fields in India are growing rapidly with OTT expansion, gaming industry, and digital marketing. NID Ahmedabad, NIFT, FTII Pune are premier institutions. Mumbai and Hyderabad dominate film/media. Freelancing is common. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b93\u20135 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b96\u201318 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b918\u201340+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Mumbai, Delhi, Bengaluru, Hyderabad; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
