    "description": "",
    "chunk_text": "Traditional Medicine Practitioners in India commonly include Ayurvedic Doctors and Homeopathic Doctors trained through BAMS or BHMS degree programs under the AYUSH medical system. These professionals diagnose and treat patients using traditional Indian and alternative medicine systems based on herbal formulations, holistic treatment methods, and lifestyle-based healing approaches. Typical daily tasks include diagnosing patient conditions through consultations, prescribing herbal or homeopathic medicines, developing treatment plans based on traditional medical frameworks, educating patients on preventive healthcare and diet, and maintaining patient records in clinics or hospitals. Important skills include patient communication, diagnostic reasoning, herbal medicine knowledge, clinical decision making, empathy, problem solving, holistic health planning, observation skills, and ethical practice. Knowledge areas include Ayurvedic or homeopathic pharmacology, human anatomy and physiology, pathology, herbal medicine systems, and preventive healthcare. Work style emphasizes compassion, patience, and holistic thinking, suiting social and investigative personalities interested in long-term patient care. In India entry requires qualifying the NEET examination and enrolling in BAMS or BHMS degree programs under AYUSH institutions. Fresh graduates typically earn 4\u20137 LPA initially, rising to 10\u201318 LPA with experience or successful private practice. Opportunities are widespread across India including rural areas where traditional medicine practitioners fill major healthcare gaps. Internationally AYUSH systems are recognized in several countries and wellness sectors but regulatory acceptance varies across regions.",
