    "description": "Gather, analyze, compile, and report information regarding individuals or organizations to clients, or detect occurrences of unlawful acts or infractions of rules in private establishment.",
    "chunk_text": "Private Detectives and Investigators (also known in India as Sr. Private Detectives and Investigators, Private Detectives and Investigators Executive) is a professional in the Protective Services & Security domain. Gather, analyze, compile, and report information regarding individuals or organizations to clients, or detect occurrences of unlawful acts or infractions of rules in private establishment. Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Physical Fitness, Surveillance, Law Knowledge, Crisis Management, Communication, Decision Making, Leadership, Ethics, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Criminal Law, Security Systems, Emergency Management, Physical Training, Public Safety. This career suits realistic and hands-on personalities who are disciplined, alert, authoritative. Protective services in India include IPS via UPSC, paramilitary via SSC/CAPF exams, armed forces via NDA/CDS. State police recruitment via state-level exams. Private security industry also large employer. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b93\u20135 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b96\u201312 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b912\u201322+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Delhi, Mumbai, All cities; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
