    "chunk_text": "Occupational Therapy Assistants (also known in India as Sr. Occupational Therapy Assistants, Occupational Therapy Assistants Executive) is a professional in the Healthcare & Medical domain. Assist occupational therapists in providing occupational therapy treatments and procedures. May, in accordance with state laws, assist in development of treatment plans, carry out routine functions, d... Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Patient Care, Medical Procedures, Empathy, Communication, Clinical Skills, Teamwork, Documentation, Infection Control, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Healthcare, Anatomy, Nutrition, First Aid, Medical Ethics. This career suits social and helping personalities who are caring, patient, responsive. Healthcare support roles require GNM, ANM, or B.Sc Nursing. Government hospitals, ESIC, and private chains are employers. Nursing council registration mandatory. Demand growing with healthcare infrastructure expansion. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b92\u20134 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b95\u20138 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b98\u201314+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Delhi, Mumbai, Chennai, Hyderabad; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
