    "chunk_text": "Protective Service Officers in India\u2019s Central Armed Police Forces include roles in organizations such as CRPF, BSF, and CISF, ranging from constables to Assistant Commandants recruited through the UPSC CAPF examination. These professionals protect national borders, guard critical infrastructure, conduct counter-insurgency and internal security operations, and support disaster response missions across the country. Day-to-day duties include patrolling sensitive areas or borders, supervising security personnel, coordinating counter-insurgency or anti-terror operations, maintaining surveillance and intelligence reporting, and managing security operations at airports, industrial facilities, or government institutions. Key skills include physical endurance, situational awareness, tactical operations planning, leadership, teamwork, crisis response, communication, discipline, risk assessment, and decision making under pressure. Knowledge areas include security operations, national defense policy, counter-terrorism strategy, criminal law basics, and disaster response management. Work style emphasizes courage, discipline, and adaptability, suited to realistic and enterprising personalities who prefer action-oriented and structured environments. In India entry is through exams such as the UPSC CAPF Assistant Commandant exam or direct recruitment for constables through force-specific selection processes. Starting salaries range roughly from 6\u201310 LPA depending on rank and allowances, rising to 20\u201330+ LPA at senior command positions with strong job stability and government benefits. Personnel are posted across India including border areas, conflict zones, airports, and major urban centers. Internationally the training aligns with security services, border protection agencies, and private security management roles.",
