    "chunk_text": "Pest Control Workers (also known in India as Sr. Pest Control Workers, Pest Control Workers Executive) is a professional in the Building & Facility Services domain. Apply or release chemical solutions or toxic gases and set traps to kill or remove pests and vermin that infest buildings and surrounding areas. Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Cleaning Techniques, Equipment Operation, Chemical Safety, Time Management, Physical Stamina, Attention to Detail, Safety Protocols, Team Coordination, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Cleaning Products, Safety Standards, Waste Management, Facilities Operations, Health Regulations. This career suits realistic and hands-on personalities who are reliable, physically active, thorough. Facility services in India organized through contract companies like Quess Corp, Sodexo, ISS. ITI certification preferred. Integrated facility management growing in IT parks, hospitals, and corporate campuses. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b91\u20133 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b94\u20136 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b96\u201310+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include All major cities; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
