    "chunk_text": "Food Preparation Workers (also known in India as Sr. Food Preparation Workers, Food Preparation Workers Executive) is a professional in the Food Service & Hospitality domain. Perform a variety of food preparation duties other than cooking, such as preparing cold foods and shellfish, slicing meat, and brewing coffee or tea. Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Food Preparation, Hygiene Standards, Customer Service, Teamwork, Speed, Creativity, Inventory Management, Menu Planning, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Culinary Arts, Food Science, Nutrition, Safety Standards, Cost Management. This career suits realistic and hands-on personalities who are hands-on, team-oriented, service-focused. Hospitality and food service in India growing with tourism and food delivery boom. NCHMCT JEE for hotel management institutes. IHM Mumbai, IHM Delhi are top government institutes. Taj, Oberoi, ITC are premium employers. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b92\u20134 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b95\u20139 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b99\u201318+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Mumbai, Delhi, Bengaluru, Goa; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
