    "description": "Operate real estate office, or work for commercial real estate firm, overseeing real estate transactions. Other duties usually include selling real estate or renting properties and arranging loans.",
    "chunk_text": "Real Estate Brokers (also known in India as Sr. Real Estate Brokers, Real Estate Brokers Executive) is a professional in the Sales & Retail domain. Operate real estate office, or work for commercial real estate firm, overseeing real estate transactions. Other duties usually include selling real estate or renting properties and arranging loans. Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Communication, Persuasion, Product Knowledge, Negotiation, CRM Tools, Target Achievement, Customer Relations, Market Analysis, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Sales Techniques, Consumer Psychology, Marketing, Product/Industry Knowledge, CRM Systems. This career suits enterprising and leadership-driven personalities who are persuasive, goal-oriented, resilient. Sales is one of the largest employment sectors in India. FMCG, BFSI, pharma, telecom, and e-commerce are heavy recruiters. Incentive-based compensation common. MBA in Sales/Marketing from IIMs or top B-schools accelerates growth. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b93\u20135 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b96\u201316 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b916\u201335+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Mumbai, Delhi, Bengaluru, Hyderabad; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
