    "baseSuitabilityScore": 85,
    "extractedSkillsCount": 10,
    "description": "Attend to live farm, ranch, open range or aquacultural animals that may include cattle, sheep, swine, goats, horses and other equines, poultry, rabbits, finfish, shellfish, and bees. Attend to animals produced for animal products, such as meat, fur, skins, feathers, eggs, milk, and honey. Duties may include feeding, watering, herding, grazing, milking, castrating, branding, de-beaking, weighing, catching, and loading animals. May maintain records on animals; examine animals to detect diseases and injuries; assist in birth deliveries; and administer medications, vaccinations, or insecticides as appropriate. May clean and maintain animal housing areas. Includes workers who shear wool from sheep and collect eggs in hatcheries.",
    "chunk_text": "Farmworkers, Farm, Ranch, and Aquacultural Animals (also known in India as Sr. Farmworkers, Farm, Ranch, and Aquacultural Animals, Farmworkers, Farm, Ranch, and Aquacultural Animals Executive) is a professional in the Agriculture, Forestry & Fishing domain. Attend to live farm, ranch, open range or aquacultural animals that may include cattle, sheep, swine, goats, horses and other equines, poultry, rabbits, finfish, shellfish, and bees. Attend to animals... Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Agronomy, Soil Science, Irrigation, Pest Management, Equipment Operation, Crop Science, Data Recording, Sustainability Practices, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Agriculture, Soil Science, Biology, Weather Patterns, Agricultural Economics. This career suits realistic and hands-on personalities who are outdoor-oriented, practical, patient. Agriculture sector employs ~50% of India's workforce. BSc/MSc Agriculture from State Agriculture Universities or IARI. ICAR-AIEEA for central agri universities. UPSC for IFS (Indian Forest Service). AgriTech startup ecosystem growing rapidly. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b92\u20134 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b95\u201312 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b912\u201322+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include Hyderabad, Pune, Delhi, Lucknow; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
