    "extractedSkillsCount": 10,
    "description": "",
    "chunk_text": "Military Officers including Indian Army Officers in India correspond to the broader occupation of commissioned military officers and include positions such as Indian Army Commissioned Officer, Technical Entry Scheme Officer, and officers commissioned through National Defence Academy (NDA) or Combined Defence Services (CDS). These professionals lead military units, plan and execute defense operations, ensure training readiness, and safeguard national security through strategic and tactical command responsibilities. Typical day-to-day activities include commanding soldiers during field operations or exercises, planning defense strategies and training programs, coordinating logistics and equipment readiness, supervising personnel and discipline within units, and participating in national security planning and crisis response. Key skills include leadership, strategic thinking, physical endurance, decision making under pressure, communication, risk assessment, teamwork, tactical planning, problem solving, and discipline. Core knowledge areas include military strategy, defense technology, geopolitics and security studies, leadership and management, and physical training sciences. Work style emphasizes discipline, resilience, courage, and responsibility, strongly suited to realistic and enterprising personalities who enjoy action-oriented leadership roles. In India entry routes include the National Defence Academy exam after 12th (PCM required for technical branches), Combined Defence Services exam after graduation, and the Technical Entry Scheme for engineering candidates. Training occurs at prestigious academies such as NDA Pune and Indian Military Academy Dehradun. Starting salaries range roughly from 10\u201312 LPA including allowances under the 7th Pay Commission, growing to 25\u201340+ LPA equivalent at colonel or higher ranks with substantial benefits and pension. Officers serve across India in postings from border areas to strategic command centers. Internationally, military leadership experience is respected in defense consulting, security strategy, and global peacekeeping operations.",
