    "id": "soc_55-1012.00",
    "title": "Indian Navy / Indian Air Force Officer",
    "category": "Defense & Aerospace Services",
    "code": "ONET 55-1012.00",
    "onet_soc_code": "55-1012.00",
    "experienceLevel": "12th Pass (Entry - Mid Level)",
    "education_required": "12th Pass",
    "transitionHorizonMonths": 6,
    "baseSuitabilityScore": 85,
    "extractedSkillsCount": 10,
    "description": "",
    "chunk_text": "Military Officers in naval and air defense roles in India include Indian Navy Officers and Indian Air Force Officers recruited through the National Defence Academy (NDA) or Air Force Common Admission Test (AFCAT). These professionals operate and manage advanced defense systems including naval vessels, submarines, fighter aircraft, and air defense networks while leading technical and operational teams responsible for national maritime and air security. Typical daily responsibilities include piloting or supervising aircraft operations, managing ship or squadron activities, conducting tactical training and simulations, coordinating defense operations with joint forces, and overseeing maintenance of advanced military equipment. Essential skills include leadership, technical aptitude, situational awareness, decision making under pressure, teamwork, navigation or flight planning, communication, problem solving, discipline, and risk management. Knowledge areas include aeronautical engineering fundamentals, navigation and maritime systems, military strategy, defense electronics, and geopolitics. Work style emphasizes high discipline, precision, and resilience, fitting realistic and investigative personalities comfortable with technology-intensive operational environments. Entry routes include NDA after 12th (PCM mandatory for flying or technical branches) or AFCAT after graduation for various officer roles. Training occurs at academies such as Air Force Academy Hyderabad and Indian Naval Academy Ezhimala. Starting compensation typically ranges around 11\u201313 LPA with allowances, rising to 30\u201345+ LPA equivalent at senior ranks with strong long-term benefits and pension. Officers are posted across strategic bases including coastal commands, airbases, and defense headquarters. Internationally, skills gained in aviation, defense technology, and command leadership translate well to aerospace, aviation management, and defense consulting sectors.",
