    "extractedSkillsCount": 10,
    "description": "",
    "chunk_text": "Ship Officers and Marine Navigators in India commonly include Merchant Navy Officers who operate commercial cargo ships, oil tankers, and international shipping vessels transporting goods across global trade routes. These professionals are responsible for navigating ships safely, supervising maritime operations, managing ship crews, ensuring compliance with international maritime regulations, and coordinating cargo logistics during voyages. Typical daily tasks include navigation planning and route monitoring, supervising loading and unloading of cargo, maintaining ship safety systems, managing crew operations and communication, and monitoring weather and maritime traffic conditions. Important skills include navigation, situational awareness, leadership, technical operations management, communication, risk assessment, decision making, teamwork, problem solving, and mechanical understanding. Knowledge areas include marine engineering fundamentals, maritime navigation systems, international maritime law, meteorology, and ship safety operations. Work style emphasizes discipline, adaptability, and resilience, suited to realistic and enterprising personalities comfortable working in challenging environments at sea for extended periods. In India entry commonly occurs through the Indian Maritime University Common Entrance Test or through sponsorship programs offered by shipping companies after completing 12th with PCM. Entry-level compensation can range from 12\u201320 LPA and may rise to 40\u201380+ LPA for senior officers such as chief engineers or captains due to international shipping salaries. Major maritime training hubs include Mumbai, Chennai, Kochi, and Visakhapatnam. Internationally this career offers strong global mobility and high earning potential because merchant shipping operates across international waters and multinational fleets.",
