    "description": "Install, repair, or adjust audio or television receivers, stereo systems, camcorders, video systems, or other electronic entertainment equipment in homes or other venues. May perform routine maintenance.",
    "chunk_text": "Audiovisual Equipment Installers and Repairers (also known in India as Sr. Audiovisual Equipment Installers and Repairers, Audiovisual Equipment Installers and Repairers Executive) is a professional in the Installation, Maintenance & Repair domain. Install, repair, or adjust audio or television receivers, stereo systems, camcorders, video systems, or other electronic entertainment equipment in homes or other venues. May perform routine maintenan... Day-to-day activities include analyzing requirements and planning deliverables, collaborating with cross-functional teams, preparing documentation and reports, applying domain expertise to solve complex challenges, and mentoring junior professionals. Core skills required include Technical Troubleshooting, Equipment Repair, Electrical Systems, Mechanical Skills, Safety Protocols, Diagnostic Skills, Blueprint Reading, Hand Tools, along with strong communication and adaptability. Foundational knowledge areas span Electrical Systems, Mechanics, Electronics, Safety Standards, Technical Systems. This career suits realistic and hands-on personalities who are hands-on, problem-solving, physically active. Maintenance and repair roles in India accessed via ITI/Polytechnic. Indian Railways, BHEL, power companies major employers. NCVT certification valued. Skilled technicians in demand in EV sector, renewables, and manufacturing hubs like Pune, Chennai, Ahmedabad. In India, freshers can expect starting salaries of \u20b92\u20134 LPA, with mid-career professionals earning \u20b95\u201311 LPA and senior roles reaching \u20b911\u201320+ LPA; stability is typically achieved within 3\u20135 years with consistent performance. Key employment hubs in India include All major cities, Industrial zones; some relocation is often necessary to access premium opportunities. Internationally, this career has strong demand in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia, with skilled worker visas (H-1B, Tier-2) and competitive salaries available for qualified professionals.",
